{"title":"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Engineer&#39;s_Induction_-_not_rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Engineer's Induction - not rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Uses_first_half_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Uses first half of Solution 1)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Faster_Alternate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Faster Alternate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb12e06e542e73a4fa3b7237d8be00b2bef219c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Matrix\" title=\"Matrix\">matrix</a> with entries as follows: for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77545605bce4aa44f33952dbe9e99446757ca9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i,i} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />; for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290ca5ca749d5895f396eb7ef64a8c042b6997fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c9a87bd132c02db4b2e65256d1fc264db0eb31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i+1,i} = m_{i,i+1} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />; all other entries in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb12e06e542e73a4fa3b7237d8be00b2bef219c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> are zero. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eacbcb991af87d495f8689ac0e952b51317dbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Determinant\" title=\"Determinant\">determinant</a> of matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb12e06e542e73a4fa3b7237d8be00b2bef219c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb2a1e3fa5bb2550e5dc5bf65b9a78fa312ec5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{8D_n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"99\" height=\"53\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Note: The determinant of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de38c39460667f504b7b57c3daa08d8d13cdaa9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and the determinant of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edad55ef85a6860138acda7544b082ae0db514ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[ {\\begin{array}{cc}  a &amp; b  \\\\  c &amp; d  \\\\  \\end{array} } \\right] = ad - bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />; for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, the determinant of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix with first row or first column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4a1da7fe36d1de76a9500123580e95d556b026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1C_1 - a_2C_2 + a_3C_3 - \\dots + (-1)^{n+1}a_nC_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"325\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c117e8403b3b9cf74d2f63f6627aa17c1995e3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is the determinant of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e694866c778641ecc749a23eb7e981abea22f50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n - 1) \\times (n - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> matrix formed by eliminating the row and column containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/869c7f930a50d2c9a990aabf372618c2d4dd7b89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}  10    \\end{vmatrix} = 10, \\quad D_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix} 10 &amp; 3  \\\\  3 &amp; 10  \\\\ \\end{vmatrix} =(10)(10) - (3)(3) = 91, \\quad D_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}  10 &amp; 3 &amp; 0  \\\\  3 &amp; 10 &amp; 3  \\\\  0 &amp; 3 &amp; 10  \\\\  \\end{vmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"622\" height=\"65\" />\nUsing the expansionary/recursive definition of determinants (also stated in the problem):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee873d548c6945b501228cb9bf289b846c86a5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{3}=\\left| {\\begin{array}{ccc}  10 &amp; 3 &amp; 0  \\\\  3 &amp; 10 &amp; 3  \\\\  0 &amp; 3 &amp; 10  \\\\  \\end{array} } \\right|=10\\left| {\\begin{array}{cc}  10 &amp; 3  \\\\  3 &amp; 10  \\\\  \\end{array} } \\right| - 3\\left| {\\begin{array}{cc}  3 &amp; 3  \\\\  0 &amp; 10  \\\\  \\end{array} } \\right| + 0\\left| {\\begin{array}{cc}  3 &amp; 10  \\\\  0 &amp; 3  \\\\  \\end{array} } \\right| = 10D_{2} - 9D_{1} = 820$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"672\" height=\"65\" />\n</p><p>This pattern repeats because the first element in the first row of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c58a6529c6704977819879f29a29869d9f8c057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is always 10, the second element is always 3, and the rest are always 0. The ten element directly expands to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/66710a954017094105fb2426dae25788f502df9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10D_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />. The three element expands to 3 times the determinant of the the matrix formed from omitting the second column and first row from the original matrix. Call this matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42b090afbc08d2df1bffb05474bf7a13d091d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42b090afbc08d2df1bffb05474bf7a13d091d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> has a first column entirely of zeros except for the first element, which is a three. A property of matrices is that the determinant can be expanded over the rows instead of the columns (still using the recursive definition as given in the problem), and the determinant found will still be the same. Thus, expanding over this first column yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d81bc0c6813bb259b739ad4cc8a873e1ebb4f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3D_{n-2} + 0(\\text{other things})=3D_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e179af5b1e40b69581bd1efab049f63186a663fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\det(X_{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> expression turns into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62ee2296b5b2baccf8132aa326d21eb9739aaa05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9D_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ae6fed6d1c12be80afdd3ab973141597a8b458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{n}=10D_{n-1}-9D_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"15\" /> holds for all n &gt; 2.\n</p><p>This equation can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2f0d09a3bcf5b1c0c8b020e7ee085f98dc9aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{n}=10(D_{n-1}-D_{n-2}) + D_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" />. This version of the equation involves the difference of successive terms of a recursive sequence. Calculating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c735cec0357d7708a0e8c8a7e266ea4530f59ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> backwards from the recursive formula and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b322f2cdf36afb6bfa1f8cafd0024a2f2fd3aad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> from the formula yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c369edb152eb6d4a92198ee87a3031b5f464a216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{0}=1, D_{4}=7381$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />. Examining the differences between successive terms, a pattern emerges. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea1fd7aaa37d2d32cf0e3d4719932b9a0635e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{0}=1=9^{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2e223aaa5df33ac963ffb3538570f8f695163b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{1}-D_{0}=10-1=9=9^{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f00d1b0fe33b4e8daf5821c858e2fae1ea51850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{2}-D_{1}=91-10=81=9^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"231\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976a7d1fa0a8cca55c3d0312f4591a7f6434300b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{3}-D_{2}=820-91=729=9^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"250\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a4b6737de1ad4a355a77f22fd8ff439cd51061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{4}-D_{3}=7381-820=6561=9^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"277\" height=\"17\" />.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0ffe3e8bf72e5529936210cc560452f45f5a791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{n}=D_{0} + 9^{1}+9^{2}+ . . . +9^{n}=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}9^{i}=\\frac{(1)(9^{n+1}-1)}{9-1}=\\frac{9^{n+1}-1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"522\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb29df59d28e9d1d922a8fc6aa69dbc4dc8c1f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{8\\frac{9^{n+1}-1}{8}+1}=\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{9^{n+1}-1+1} = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{9^{n+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"367\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>This is an infinite <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric series\">geometric series</a> with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d566f72db7c1e787d2817d1023c750de6593928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594c8b267069448b58fe77ad60497eb30f763a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6501bab6b897aef34928fdc3b6beeade6768923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{1-\\frac{1}{9}}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{\\frac{8}{9}}=\\frac{9}{(81)(8)}=\\frac{1}{(9)(8)}=\\frac{1}{72}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"294\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e7dbf4642646cb7526dfd4e89ec4f78731d3157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q = 1 + 72 = \\boxed{073}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Engineer.27s_Induction_-_not_rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Engineer's_Induction_-_not_rigorous)\">Solution 2 (Engineer's Induction - not rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Engineer&#39;s Induction - not rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89da956bc2b5c08b018ca6854682346c36169726.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"Manually, we can find \\( D_1 = 10 \\), \\( D_2 = 91 \\), \\( D_3 = 820 \\).   \\[ \\frac{1}{8D_1+1} = \\frac{1}{81}, \\quad \\frac{1}{8D_2+1} = \\frac{1}{729}, \\quad \\frac{1}{8D_3+1} = \\frac{1}{6561}. \\]   We notice that \\( 81 = 9^2 \\), \\( 729 = 9^3 \\), and \\( 6561 = 9^4 \\), and believe that this cannot be a coincidence.    Assume \\( \\frac{1}{8D_n+1} = \\frac{1}{9^{n+1}} \\). Then this problem asks us to find the sum of a geometric series with first term \\( \\frac{1}{81} \\) and common ratio \\( \\frac{1}{9} \\).   \\[ \\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{1 - \\frac{1}{9}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{\\frac{8}{9}} = \\frac{1}{72}. \\]    Thus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{73}\\).\" width=\"540\" height=\"318\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Uses_first_half_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Uses_first_half_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 3 (Uses first half of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Uses first half of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From Solution 1, \\( D_n = 10D_{n-1} - 9D_{n-2} \\). From Solution 1, we also know \\( D_2 = 91 \\).  \nWe can manually compute \\( D_1 = 10 \\). Iterating backwards, \\(D_0 = 1 \\).\n</p><p>The characteristic polynomial of this recurrence is  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc4bb5290d349b9526d837cc9185334dba17d18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - 10x + 9,\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />  \nwhich has roots \\( 1 \\) and \\( 9 \\).  \nTherefore, the explicit formula for \\( D_n \\) is:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dca22b91bc19c0429b1a674c0e064c5f8789a42d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n = \\alpha_1 + 9^n \\alpha_2.\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />  \n</p><p>We can solve for \\( \\alpha_1 \\) and \\( \\alpha_2 \\) by setting \\( n=0 \\) and \\( n=1 \\) respectively. This gives the following equations:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3239772cdfc22d361b2509767b632142a3935874.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha_1 + \\alpha_2 = 1,\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06d96b052cfd06e7a300450894e74d53ac51413.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha_1 + 9\\alpha_2 = 10.\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />  \n</p><p>Solving these equations, we find  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d531efc2a0da2858978f3c754dc3aeb7e603e6c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha_1 = -\\frac{1}{8}, \\quad \\alpha_2 = \\frac{9}{8}.\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />  \n</p><p>Substituting these back into the explicit formula, we find  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165b5ee792709b7f7b66dac899d3490f2d9cac24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n = \\frac{9^{n+1} - 1}{8}.\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"39\" />  \n</p><p>Notice that  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/771eb987b04c10e3f50eafabee3709d873538194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{8D_{n+1} + 1} = 9^{-(n+1)}.\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"41\" />  \n</p><p>The summation asks us to find the sum of a geometric series with ratio \\( \\frac{1}{9} \\) and first term \\( \\frac{1}{81} \\).  \nThe sum of this series is  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01633b7eeca6d33002a0b9dd60772cb2cc58d56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{1 - \\frac{1}{9}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{81}}{\\frac{8}{9}} = \\frac{1}{72}.\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"47\" />  \n</p><p>Thus, the answer is  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0c1085eb3ba5eb6376bc00e7ea24690c680775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{73}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Faster_Alternate\">Faster Alternate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Faster Alternate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Optionally, one can notice that the recursive relation is a first order non-homogenous relation in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfec438a8b811f90ccbeba10aedd40418921be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = ra_{n-1} + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />. So, to solve this (and all other first orders), we first need to find a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for which\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33daf767cd7fb6739be10891a71fac567cf23681.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L = rL+c\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>in which we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512ba398122ffcb85fd0f2d398d4b88670fadd99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L = 9L+1\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf8493943006af85248599b2cca38e2da30f966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L = -\\frac{1}{8}\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is called the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e9805b33454e78086220c8a04571fa949780a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Equilibrium Point}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"17\" /> of a recurrence relation. Its property satisfies:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b664b4cdc05514b0beff4f4a3b0d177e2981d5ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n - L = r(D_{n-1}-L)\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cecee5354ba9aa0e8408d80dc8f1a596ee56ea07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n + \\frac{1}{8} = 9(D_{n-1}+\\frac{1}{8})\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67ae9db952bba6b7ec3dc834e824bd1e750c5e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = D_n + \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />. The result is a geometric sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80d10236fcccf69713d1d3b92bb95092cf16136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. The explicit rule for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is just \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d02933dc677e20884f2c96931f978af338687b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\frac{81}{8} \\cdot 9^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />. Conversion back to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eacbcb991af87d495f8689ac0e952b51317dbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> can be done quite easily.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358815eb571eec669f44d939a3c88c8eeacb4f66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{9^{n+1}}{8}\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cca4fe3c3b70140a86838a1bf868d603051708a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_n = \\frac{9^{n+1} - 1}{8}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>The explicit rule has been reached and one can simply continue as follows.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II\" title=\"2011 AIME II\">2011 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164335\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.073 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 493/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16340/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.742      1 -total\n 56.72%    7.794      1 Template:AIME_box\n 41.73%    5.735      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9216:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164335 and revision id 282657. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}